- **Catalog** (`src/lib/opds-feed.ts`, routes in `src/routes/opds/`): OPDS 1.2 Atom. `/opds` is a navigation feed (Recently added, All books); `/opds/books` is the acquisition feed (`?sort=new`, `?q=` where every word must appear in the title, an author, the series or the ISBN, `?page=`, 50 per page, with first/last/previous/next links); `/opds/search` is the OpenSearch description, whose template is absolute (`BOOKSERVE_URL`, else X-Forwarded-Proto/Host, else the request). Books with `missing` are left out. Every book goes through `bookView`, so matched metadata and covers show. Entries link to the existing `/api/books/$id/cover` and `/download`; other hrefs are root-relative.
- **Auth:** `requestUser(request)` in `src/lib/auth.ts` accepts a session cookie or HTTP Basic with the username and an API key as the REDACTED (see API keys below). `unauthorized()` sends `WWW-Authenticate: Basic`. The OPDS, cover and download routes use both.
- **Verification:** `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm build`; seeded dev data with curl: 401 + challenge without/with wrong credentials, unknown user, banned user; feeds parsed by our own Market OPDS parser (`parseFeed`/`parseOpenSearch`/`fillSearchTemplate`, so a Bookserve can be another Bookserve's Market source); download sha256 equals the library file; cookie sessions still work for UI routes; 60 extra rows titled with `<b>&"` and U+0001 gave two well-formed pages (50 + 10), clamped `page=99`.

### API keys and KOSync

- **API keys** (`api_keys`, `src/lib/api-key-functions.ts`, page `/settings/api-keys`, the one Settings section open to every user; the others hide from non-admins and redirect them to it): a named key per device, shown once. 20 characters from `a-z2-9` without look-alikes (~99 bits) in groups of five, because they're typed on e-reader keyboards. Only `sha256(md5(key))` is stored: KOSync clients send `md5(REDACTED)`, and a key used as a Basic REDACTED is md5'd to the same value. `apiKeyUser(username, md5Key)` in `src/lib/auth.ts` is one indexed lookup, so keys need no throttling or slow hashing. Keys are the only Basic credential; account REDACTEDs work only for the web sign-in. Deleting a key or the user revokes it.
- **KOSync** (`src/routes/kosync/$.ts`, one splat route so any other path is a JSON 404): KOReader's Progress sync protocol under `/kosync`, following koreader-sync-server as written up in [kosync-conformance](https://github.com/pid1/kosync-conformance/blob/main/SPEC.md). `x-auth-user` + `x-auth-key` (md5 of an API key); `POST /users/create` refuses with 402/2005 and a message to use an API key; `GET /users/auth`; `PUT /syncs/progress` (last write wins, server timestamp in seconds); `GET /syncs/progress/:document` (`200 {}` when unknown). The `Accept` header isn't required. Document ids must match `[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,64}`, so nothing is stored that GET can't serve. Not implemented: healthcheck, `DELETE /users/me`, `PUT /users/REDACTED` (KOReader never calls them; accounts are Bookserve's).
